{"id":727,"date":"2015-10-21T12:58:51","date_gmt":"2015-10-21T12:58:51","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/www.eleanorgail.co.uk\/?p=727"},"modified":"2021-02-03T16:08:10","modified_gmt":"2021-02-03T16:08:10","slug":"lovely-lace-and-cad-the-dandy-a-whimsical-wedding-at-bryngarw","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/eleanorgail.co.uk\/wedding-planner\/lovely-lace-and-cad-the-dandy-a-whimsical-wedding-at-bryngarw\/","title":{"rendered":"Linda &#038; Victor&#8217;s wedding at Bryngarw House."},"content":{"rendered":"<p>A whimsical and intimate wedding at Bryngarw House, S. Wales where Linda and Victor married in a western civil ceremony while honouring their Chinese heritage and traditions.<\/p>\n<p>Beautiful gardens, the feeling of being outdoors and exclusive use was really important to this elegant couple and Eleanor Gail found the perfect wedding venue in Bryngarw, Bridgend. They said \u201cI Do\u201d under a floral arch in front of floor to ceiling windows in an emotional ceremony, surrounded by their closest family and friends. White, soft greens complimented the \u2018orangery\u2019 feel while champagne gold ensured there was plenty of glamour.<\/p>\n<p>The bride wore a stunning off-shoulder, long sleeved lace gown with a train and the groom wore a hand-made navy Cad &amp; The Dandy suit.<\/p>\n<p>The photographs are by kind permission of the Bride and Groom and we\u2019re chuffed to pieces they allowed us to share them with you.<\/p>\n<p>&#8220;Thanks for everything, Gail. We had an amazing wedding day that we can remember forever. &#8221; Linda &amp; Victor Chen.x.<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.eleanorgail.co.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/10\/1.jpg\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-749\" src=\"http:\/\/www.eleanorgail.co.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/10\/1-300x200.jpg\" alt=\"1\" width=\"300\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https:\/\/eleanorgail.co.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/10\/1-200x133.jpg 200w, https:\/\/eleanorgail.